## Key design decisions (diverge from ref commit `18b3312e`, deliberately)
1. **Slice-3-only.** Ref commit combined slices 3+4+5 (deleted IPC, dropped ~2537 lines of IPC tests, rewired renderer/preload, moved domain to `src/server/`). Per task constraint "No renderer/handler-deletion (slice 5)" + "never drop functionality", I kept IPC + all 5 test files + domain in `src/main/`. Matches the landed slice-3 convention (`@slayzone/automations`).
2. **Injection via `app-deps.ts` (not module-global, not ctx).** Found the codebase's purpose-built mechanism: electron-coupled domain ops are injected into transport via `app-deps.ts` setter/getter (the chat router does exactly this with `setChatDeps`/`getChatDeps`). `IntegrationOps` is the same category as `ChatDeps`, so `setIntegrationOps`/`getIntegrationOps` is the consistent home — supersedes the ctx-injection idea from the plan. `ctx.automationEngine` is reserved for the small decoupled structural interface; not appropriate for a 44-method electron-coupled bundle.

